- geometry.xyz is a molecule configuration in free space that was relaxed in siesta PBE GGA
- relaxed_main_conf_4.xyz is after the relaxation with ORCA using R2SCAN-3C TightSCF Tight. I'm currently running the functional_scan analysis on this geometry (hoping to get ferromagnetic ground state)


From running geometry.xyz I get that the energies are as follows:

pbe
  broken_symmetry    -2075.116418045908 Eh
  high_spin          -2075.116394214763 Eh
  ΔE (HS - BS)       0.000023831145 Eh  =  0.6485 meV

r2scan
  broken_symmetry    -2076.605937530752 Eh
  high_spin          -2076.605840766440 Eh
  ΔE (HS - BS)       0.000096764312 Eh  =  2.6331 meV

b3lyp
  broken_symmetry    -2076.441186991280 Eh
  high_spin          -2076.441145548622 Eh
  ΔE (HS - BS)       0.000041442658 Eh  =  1.1277 meV

pbe0
  broken_symmetry    -2075.281425081102 Eh
  high_spin          -2075.281357805090 Eh
  ΔE (HS - BS)       0.000067276012 Eh  =  1.8307 meV

r2scan0
  broken_symmetry    -2076.353180635525 Eh
  high_spin          -2076.352768065251 Eh
  ΔE (HS - BS)       0.000412570274 Eh  =  11.2266 meV

cam_b3lyp
  broken_symmetry    -2076.537696701726 Eh
  high_spin          -2076.537587831526 Eh
  ΔE (HS - BS)       0.000108870200 Eh  =  2.9625 meV


The radiclas are consistently antiferromagnetically coupled (broken symmetry) for all functionals.
The radical sites tend to be more localized (higher Mulliken spin density) when increasing the complexity of teh functional. 
I would not take r2scan0 too seriously because S^2 differs too much from teh expected value (2 for high spin and 1 for broken symmetry).

